  <!-- SECTION 9 — FAQ ACCORDION -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="c">
      <span class="eye">Common Questions</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="faq-h2">Questions Buyers Ask About SDF Clothing</h2>
      <p class="lead">Click any question to read the answer.</p>

      <div class="faq-wrap">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a1">
            <span class="faq-q">What is the minimum order quantity?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a1" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a"><strong>300 pieces per style</strong> — across OEM, private label, CMT, and ODM. Size distribution within the 300 pieces is fully flexible. Multiple styles on the same purchase order each carry their own 300-piece minimum. A brand ordering two styles at 300 pieces each — 600 total — is a completely standard first order. No higher MOQ for new clients, no trial order surcharges.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a2">
            <span class="faq-q">What makes SDF different from other garment manufacturers in Bangladesh?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a2" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Three things come up most often from new clients. First, the <strong>300-piece MOQ</strong> — most Bangladesh garment factories start at 500 to 1,000 pieces. Second, <strong>full-chain GOTS certification</strong> — many factories use organic cotton but cannot issue the GOTS certificate of conformity that legally authorises your organic labelling claim. We can, because our certification covers every stage from raw fibre to finished garment. Third, <strong>EU EPR 2026 readiness</strong> — we generate Digital Product Passport data files as standard for EU orders. Most Bangladesh garment manufacturers are not doing this yet. On top of those, direct factory access means you see real pricing — no agent margin layered on top.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a3">
            <span class="faq-q">What is the production lead time from brief to shipment?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a3" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Proto sample: <strong>14 days</strong> from confirmed brief, DHL Express to your door. Pre-production sample: 10 days after proto approval. Bulk production: <strong>30 to 45 days</strong> from PP sample sign-off depending on category. Total first-order time from brief to FOB Chittagong: 55 to 65 days. Repeat orders run faster because fabric and PP samples are already approved. Ocean freight to EU ports takes an additional 22 to 28 days. Air freight to major EU and UK airports takes 4 to 5 days for urgent orders.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a4">
            <span class="faq-q">Do EU and UK brands pay import duty on garments from SDF Clothing?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a4" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a"><strong>No.</strong> Bangladesh holds EU GSP EBA (Everything But Arms) status — 0% import duty on most apparel and garments (HS chapters 61 and 62) into all 27 EU member states and the UK under the UK GSP scheme. The standard EU MFN duty on clothing is 12% of CIF value — on a €100,000 order that is €12,000 saved compared to sourcing from China or other non-GSP countries. We prepare EUR.1 Movement Certificates for every EU and UK shipment. See our <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-italy/">Italy</a>, <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-germany/">Germany</a>, or <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-uk/">UK pages</a> for country-specific customs detail.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a5">
            <span class="faq-q">Can SDF Clothing produce GOTS certified organic garments?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a5" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes — and the distinction matters. We hold <strong>full-chain GOTS certification</strong>: from raw organic cotton sourcing through spinning, dyeing, cutting, sewing, and finishing at our Dhaka factory. Transaction certificates are issued at each stage. The GOTS certificate of conformity we provide with your order is the legal document that authorises your organic labelling claim in EU, UK, and USA markets. A factory that buys organic cotton fabric but lacks GOTS scope certification cannot give you this — and without it, you cannot legally label your garments as organic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a6">
            <span class="faq-q">Does SDF Clothing work with startup fashion brands?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a6" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes. The 300-piece MOQ exists because smaller brands deserve direct factory access too. A founder placing their debut collection at 300 pieces per style gets the same factory, the same certifications, the same quality control, and the same compliance documentation as a brand ordering 50,000 pieces. Price per piece is different with volume — the production standard is not. We have worked with brands from their first-ever order through to large repeat accounts. Both matter to us.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a7">
            <span class="faq-q">Can I visit the factory in Bangladesh?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a7" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes. Factory visits are welcome for verified business partners — we encourage them. Third-party social and environmental audits at our facility are fully supported: SGS, Bureau Veritas, and Intertek all conduct audits here. If your retail buyer requires a specific audit format, we work with you to schedule it. We have nothing to hide. Factory transparency is a basic expectation of doing business with international brands — not something we offer selectively.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

